WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
Next, let's talk about the four basic steps to first aid care.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.120
Step one is scene safety.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.240
Your very first priority is your own safety and the patient's.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.440
Scan the area for environmental hazards

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.160
like fire, traffic, or water.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.959
If the scene is unsafe, do not approach.

00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:22.600
Just call for professional help and wait for them to arrive.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.320
Remember, you can't help if you're hurt.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.160
This is also a good time to put on any personal protective

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.639
equipment if available.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.520
If you must move the person, either to perform CPR

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.799
or get them to safety, do it quickly.

00:00:34.799 --> 00:00:36.639
If you suspect a neck or spinal injury

00:00:36.639 --> 00:00:38.240
and have a second person to help,

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.279
try to protect their head and neck while you move them.

00:00:41.279 --> 00:00:43.880
Step two is to identify the emergency.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.599
Remember, people won't always be able to tell you

00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:48.240
that something is wrong.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.200
Check their responsiveness and breathing

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.320
and observe them for any sudden changes

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.439
in their appearance or behavior.

00:00:54.439 --> 00:00:56.959
If the person is responsive, introduce yourself

00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:58.480
and ask if you can help.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.840
If they are unresponsive, we assume consent,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.599
meaning we act as if they want our help.

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:08.080
Step three is to call 911 and get an AED.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.720
If there are others around, tell someone specifically

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.959
to call 911 and have them find an AED.

00:01:13.959 --> 00:01:17.760
If you are alone, call 911 and place them on speakerphone.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.000
Step four is to provide care.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.760
You are essentially the caretaker

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.360
until professional help takes over the scene.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.239
In the next few slides, we're going to walk through

00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:27.959
exactly what that care looks like

00:01:27.959 --> 00:01:29.919
for different injuries and emergencies.

